§ `s 3 -- tax-free threshold`

#ASSERT `the tax-free threshold` EQUALS 18200

§ `Schedule 7 Part I -- which table applies to the year`

#ASSERT `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` 2022 EQUALS `not covered` `the deposited compilations have no Schedule 7 table for a year of income before 2023-24`
#ASSERT `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` 2023 EQUALS `answered` `Part I, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
#ASSERT `the Part II table applicable to the year of income` 2022 EQUALS `not covered` `the deposited compilations have no Schedule 7 table for a year of income before 2023-24`
#ASSERT `the Part II table applicable to the year of income` 2023 EQUALS `answered` `Part II, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
#ASSERT `the Part III table applicable to the year of income` 2023 EQUALS `answered` `Part III, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
#ASSERT `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` 2024 EQUALS `answered` `Part I, for the 2024-25 or 2025-26 year of income`
#ASSERT `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` 2025 EQUALS `answered` `Part I, for the 2024-25 or 2025-26 year of income`
#ASSERT `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` 2026 EQUALS `answered` `Part I, for the 2026-27 year of income`
#ASSERT `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` 2033 EQUALS `answered` `Part I, for the 2027-28 year of income or a later year of income`

§ `s 3 -- second and third resident personal tax rates`

#ASSERT `the second resident personal tax rate for` 2024 EQUALS `answered` (30%)
#ASSERT `the third resident personal tax rate for` 2027 EQUALS `answered` (37%)
#ASSERT `the second resident personal tax rate for` 2023 EQUALS `answered` (32.5%)
#ASSERT `the third resident personal tax rate for` 2023 EQUALS `answered` (37%)
#ASSERT `the second resident personal tax rate for` 2022 EQUALS `not covered` `the deposited compilations have no Schedule 7 table for a year of income before 2023-24`

§ `Schedule 7 Part I -- the three resident tables`

#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 18200 `for` 2024 EQUALS `answered` 0
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 45000 `for` 2024 EQUALS `answered` 4288
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 135000 `for` 2024 EQUALS `answered` 31288
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 190000 `for` 2024 EQUALS `answered` 51638
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 250000 `for` 2024 EQUALS `answered` 78638
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 71500 `for` 2026 EQUALS `answered` 11970
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 71500 `for` 2027 EQUALS `answered` 11702
-- 2023-24 (Compilation No. 62: 19% to $45,000, 32.5% to $120,000, 37% to $180,000, 45% above). c045: 9,300 x 19% = 1,767.
-- 45,000: 26,800 x 19% = 5,092; 120,000: + 75,000 x 32.5% = 24,375: 29,467; 180,000: + 60,000 x 37% = 22,200: 51,667;
-- 200,000: + 9,000: 60,667.
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 27500 `for` 2023 EQUALS `answered` 1767
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 45000 `for` 2023 EQUALS `answered` 5092
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 120000 `for` 2023 EQUALS `answered` 29467
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 180000 `for` 2023 EQUALS `answered` 51667
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 200000 `for` 2023 EQUALS `answered` 60667
#ASSERT `the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` 27500 `for` 2022 EQUALS `not covered` `the deposited compilations have no Schedule 7 table for a year of income before 2023-24`

§ `s 3 -- prescribed non-resident`

#ASSERT `a prescribed non-resident` `a non-resident earning $30,000`
#ASSERT NOT (`a prescribed non-resident` `a non-resident all year paid a Social Security pension`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a prescribed non-resident` `an arrival in October 2024, pro-rated threshold $13,650 (assumed input)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a prescribed non-resident` `a non-resident all year paid a Social Security benefit under Part 2.12`)

§ `s 16 -- eligible pensioner`

#ASSERT `an eligible pensioner` `an arrival who is an eligible pensioner`
#ASSERT NOT (`an eligible pensioner` `an arrival paid a Social Security benefit under Part 2.12`)

§ `s 18 -- part-year residency period`

#ASSERT `there is a part-year residency period for` `an arrival in October 2024, pro-rated threshold $13,650 (assumed input)`
#ASSERT NOT (`there is a part-year residency period for` `an arrival who is an eligible pensioner`)
#ASSERT NOT (`there is a part-year residency period for` `Chloe, 2024-25 return (c048)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`there is a part-year residency period for` `an arrival during July 2024`)
#ASSERT NOT (`there is a part-year residency period for` `a departure during July 2024`)
#ASSERT `there is a part-year residency period for` `a departure during December 2024, pro-rated threshold $9,100 (assumed input)`
#ASSERT `there is a part-year residency period for` `an arrival paid a Social Security benefit under Part 2.12`

